The ratio should come DOWN but NOT to 1. Part of the boundary step is real: a
multi-year composite joins the end of one year to the start of the next, so if
productivity changed the two ends genuinely differ. Regressed on the interannual
trend the step has slope -1.31, against the -1 the compositing predicts. A ratio
near 1 would mean that signal had been erased too -- which is what `--recon
harmonic` does. See docs/13_phenology_year_boundary.md.

